| !Run for !fheroes2 - RISC OS port of fheroes2 (Heroes of Might and Magic II engine)
| Built with GCCSDK GCC 10.2 (arm-riscos-gnueabihf), statically linked with
| riscos-mesa's SDL2 and converted to an Absolute (AIF) file, so
| !SharedLibs isn't needed.

Set fheroes2$Dir <Obey$Dir>
IconSprites <fheroes2$Dir>.!Sprites

| --- Game data --------------------------------------------------------
| fheroes2 needs the data of the original game (or its free demo): the
| DATA and MAPS directories (plus ANIM and MUSIC if you have them). Put
| them inside this application, next to this file, or anywhere else and
| *Set fheroes2$Data to that directory (e.g. in your !Boot).

| --- Threads ----------------------------------------------------------
| The game uses threads (UnixLib). PThreadTicker keeps them running while
| the game waits for the desktop. Loaded from !System if there, else ours.
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 IfThere System:Modules.PThrTicker Then RMLoad System:Modules.PThrTicker
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 RMLoad <fheroes2$Dir>.PThrTicker

| --- Sound ------------------------------------------------------------
| Sound goes through SharedSoundBuffer, StreamManager and SharedSound
| (in !System), mixed with other programs' sound. SharedSound is part of
| RISC OS; SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager are in ssb.zip from
| https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html. Without them the
| game plays silently. The music is MIDI, played by the game itself
| through the SoundFont in files.soundfonts.
RMEnsure SharedSound 1.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSound Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSound
RMEnsure StreamManager 0.03 IfThere System:Modules.StreamMan Then RMLoad System:Modules.StreamMan
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSBuffer Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSBuffer

| --- Logging ----------------------------------------------------------
| Normally nothing is logged. For a log in <Wimp$ScrapDir>.fheroes2log
| (useful when reporting a problem), remove the | from the next line.
| Set fheroes2$LogOn 1
Unset fheroes2$Log
If "<fheroes2$LogOn>"<>"" Then Set fheroes2$Log /|<Wimp$ScrapDir>/fheroes2log
Unset fheroes2$LogOn

| --- Memory -----------------------------------------------------------
| The C heap goes in dynamic areas ("fheroes2 Heap"), so the WimpSlot only
| holds the program and its stack.
WimpSlot -min 24000K -max 24000K

Do Run <fheroes2$Dir>.fheroes2 %*0
